        <description>&lt;p&gt;The front page gains the Federation tab: a card for every system that has Spire on it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Added&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;**Federation surface**: the main window now switches between Apps, Endpoints, and Federation. The Federation page shows a card per machine — This Mac&amp;#x27;s card carries its identity, version, endpoint, Place a Model, and what&amp;#x27;s placed; every fleet machine&amp;#x27;s card shows live reachability, its installed Spire build, and the roles its endpoint reports, checked over the same trusted channel the fleet updater uses.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The machine list is data: &lt;code&gt;Federation/machines.json&lt;/code&gt; in Spire&amp;#x27;s data folder, seeded with the fleet and editable. Paired machines will feed these same cards when pairing ships.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Changed&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Placing a model no longer requires the Settings window — the same form lives on the Federation page&amp;#x27;s This Mac card (Settings keeps it too; both are one implementation).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;</description></item>
